WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.334
Republicans defended
Congressman Paul Gosar

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:06.267
after he was formally
censured by the House

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.467
for tweeting a violent video
targeting a colleague.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.601
Meanwhile, former
President Trump sat down

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.901
for a truly insane interview
with MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell,

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:16.267
where they continued
to spread their election lies.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.834
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:22.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:24.734
Watching our two political
parties right now

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:27.968
is very much like watching two
completely alternate realities

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.501
or like watching two teams
on the same field

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:31.901
play completely
different sports,

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:33.767
like if the Jets
showed up to a game

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.367
against the Patriots
in soccer gear

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.667
and loudly complained
every time they were tackled.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.634
"I'm sorry
when you said football,

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:43.200
you meant American football?"

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.434
We wrote that last night
and then, you know,

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:48.801
then Jets show up
in vaccine news as well.

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:53.634
We have no bad -- no idea how
badly they're going to take it.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.334
For example, on the one hand,

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.133
you had President Biden
signing into law

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:59.501
a wildly popular
bipartisan infrastructure bill

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:00.968
that will invest over
a trillion dollars

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.467
in everything from roads
and bridges

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.067
to broadband
to electric vehicles.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.400
And the best part was
he didn't do that dumb thing

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.267
Trump used to do where he'd hold
up the bill for the cameras.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:12.767
Like a judge at the Olympics,

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:15.801
holding up a 10
after a floor routine.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.400
That's a joke
from our new segment,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.834
Remember That?

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.167
Remember That?

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.234
When the president used

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.200
to show off the bill
for the cameras,

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.200
like he was a waiter
at a restaurant

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.434
that had the specials written on
a chalkboard?

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:31.767
Was he signing a bill
or doing story time

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:34.033
at a local library.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:36.200
With that said,
can you imagine Donald Trump

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.467
reading a book to kids?

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.834
That's a joke
from our new segment.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:42.334
Imagine That?

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:43.367
Can you imagine that?

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.567
Donald Trump reading to kids

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.200
what would most certainly
be one of his books.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.801
So the three key deals,

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.367
the three keys
to any successful deal,

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:55.534
one, think big,
two, maximize your options,

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:59.067
and three, know a guy
who knows a guy

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:02.234
who knows a guy with mob ties.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:04.767
This has been Imagine That
within Remember That?

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:11.000
I will say one quick thing
about the Biden bill signing.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.200
And this is independent
of Biden.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.968
Why do they always
give the most powerful man

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:17.601
in the world
a tiny little schoolboy desk?

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.601
Just because that was
the right size desk

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:22.634
for what counted
as tall in 1776

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:24.167
doesn't mean we can't upgrade.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.334
You guys couldn't
find something

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:26.767
a little more suited
to the presidency?

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.200
Where is he going to do
the next bill signing?

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.868
Crammed into
a middle seat in coach?

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.167
Point is that's
what Democrats are up to.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.934
Republicans, meanwhile,
spent their Wednesday

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.100
defending one of their
most unhinged members,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.467
Arizona Congressman Paul Gosar,
who was censured by the House

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:43.000
for tweeting out a violent video
that targeted a colleague.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.501
A dramatic and historic day

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.834
at the US Capitol as the House
voted to censure

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.868
Congressman Paul Gosar

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.634
over a violent video
he posted on social media.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:54.767
The Arizona Republican becomes
the first member of Congress

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.734
to be simultaneously censured

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.701
and stripped
of his committee post.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:01.734
The Photoshopped video shows
Gosar appearing to kill

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:04.801
Democratic colleague
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.834
and then heading
for President Biden

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.133
while wielding two swords.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:11.400
No matter how much the left
tries to quiet me,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.667
I will continue to speak out.

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:15.667
If I must join
Alexander Hamilton

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:18.667
the first person attempted
to be censored by this House,

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.267
so be it, it is done.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.801
Well, this probably
doesn't need to be said,

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.234
but you're not
Alexander Hamilton.

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:27.000
For one thing, I would be
terrified to hear you rap.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.334
♪ My name is Paul,
and I'm here to say ♪

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.934
♪ I forgot
what I was here to say ♪

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:33.167
Second,
I love when these idiots

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:35.601
try to sound smart
and adopt a defiant tone

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:38.334
by using dramatic language
like, "so be it, it is done."

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:40.567
Like you don't sound
like a founding father,

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:42.501
and you sound like cousin Greg.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:46.601
If it is to be said,
so it be -- so it is.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.534
Guys, we have been watching
a lot of "Succession"

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:52.067
and let me just say I still
haven't seen Sunday's episode

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.267
and I've been trying
to make it all week

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:54.334
without any spoilers.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.501
You know how hard that is?

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.934
It's like trying
to make it through "Wipeout"

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.567
without getting knocked
into the water

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:00.834
by a giant piece of foam,

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:03.300
an obstacle course that
ironically looks like something

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.033
Logan Roy would make
his children do as a punishment.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:09.667
Do the obstacle course!

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:11.667
Duck, Tom, Duck.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.434
So Gosar compared himself
to Hamilton

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:18.734
for tweeting out
a violent video

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:20.534
targeting a colleague,
and by the way,

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:23.367
to Republicans complaining
that this is a waste of time,

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:25.434
this whole thing
would have been much easier

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:26.834
and taken up much less time

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:28.334
if you've just been willing
to step forward

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.000
and say it was
a deeply stupid tweet.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.234
But to be fair,
he is a deeply stupid man.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.834
Instead, we all had
to be subjected

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.300
to the theater
of the aggrieved

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.667
from the dumbest people
in politics.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:40.968
Take, for example,
what I like to call

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:43.968
the "Erts," Louie Gohmert
and Lauren Boebert,

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.968
whose last names
both sound like insults.

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:48.267
Boebert sounds like something
a New Yorker would yell

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:51.634
at a out of towner who stands
at the top of the escalator.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:53.467
"Hey, get out of the way,
you Boebert.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:56.701
People got jobs in this city!"

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:58.234
We've said this before,
but her name sounds

00:04:58.234 --> 00:05:02.167
like a Dilbert character
who refuses to get vaccinated.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:03.300
The joke would be
something dumb

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.901
